    "result_text": "All tests green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole test class passes). \n\n## Summary\n\nI added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` field that renders the stored E.164 telephone for humans, while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nThe codebase's established pattern is that derived owner attributes are `@Transient` getters on the `Owner` model that MapStruct auto-maps into the generated DTO, each delegating to a small static helper (like `RegionResolver`, `LuhnCheckDigit`, `AgeBand`). I followed that pattern exactly:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `telephoneDisplay` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the property.\n- **`Owner.getTelephoneDisplay()`** \u2014 new `@Transient` getter delegating to the formatter; MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n- **`model/TelephoneFormatter`** \u2014 new static helper owning the display responsibility: splits off the country calling code, then groups the national digits in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`).\n- **`model/CountryCallingCode`** \u2014 extracted the country-code knowledge (which codes exist + their national-number lengths) into a single shared source.\n- **`TelephoneNormalizer`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `CountryCallingCode` for its national-length validation instead of its own private copy of the `{\"1\":10,\"61\":9}` table, so the country-code data now lives in exactly one place.\n\nEach unit keeps a single responsibility: `CountryCallingCode` holds the data, `TelephoneFormatter` does presentation, `TelephoneNormalizer` does parsing/validation, and `Owner` just exposes the derived value \u2014 no duplication and nothing turned into a catch-all.\n\nThe acceptance test feeds `\"0412 345 678\"`, and the response now returns `telephone = \"+61412345678\"` and `telephoneDisplay = \"+61 412 345 678\"`.",
